A||||28||Leadfoot||Anyone else fedup with incorrect drive-thru orders?!||||8||
Z||000000||Leadfoot||09-17-2001||06:21 PM||||What gives?  Just today I stopped at BBK to get a wopper, coke and onion rings.  As the guy was filling my order I noticed he put fries in my bag. WTF! I yelled out that I ordered onion rings.  The bastard gave me a dirty look and was mummbling some jibberish.  This is not the first time this has happened.  About 3 out of every 4 times I go to BBK (doesn't matter which one) they always give me fries instead of the onion rings.  If you think McD is any better you better guess again.  Everytime I order a big breakfast deluxe they always forget my hash browns.  Last time they did that to me I asked for a refund.  Maybe this is a sign that I should give up fast food?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000001||Cheever3000||09-17-2001||06:34 PM||||You got that right.  I do a lot of fast-food drive-thru's (that's life in the big city, and the hurry-up millenium), and almost <I>never</I> do they get it right.  I guess they're in as much a hurry as I am, and they don't care much if it's right or not.  When I get good service, I try to take it to PlanetFeedback.com, but it's been so long I don't even know if that site still exists.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||09-17-2001||06:36 PM||||they all suck anymore. Most of the time its faster to park and go in.  McD's 30 seconds or less is more like 30 minutes. I had a friend that fell asleep in line sitting in his car. They had to come and wake him up, LOL.||||reg||1
