Z||000008||wkayl||09-17-2001||09:46 PM||||I hate raw onions.  That is why I don't use McD's drive through (they use chpopped).  I use Wendys or BK because when (not if) the mess up, the rings are easier to throw away.  What realy twists them is when I order a burger wiyh out onions and then order onion rings.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_2.jpg">    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/usa1017[1].gif">   <BR>Dnyee's 88 Formula, Casey's 86GT, Wayne's 86GT.  <BR>We consider my wife as being "Fiero Challenged"||||reg||1
Z||000009||Formula88||09-17-2001||10:02 PM||||It's not just fast food drive through.  It's a problem with people in general who don't give a flyin' crap about the job they're doing.  Maybe that's because minimum wage jobs are crap...  I dunno.  When I worked for Micky D's when I was in high school, we worked hard and actually gave a damn.  Of course, that was so long ago that McDonald's actually "cooked" their food sometime in the recent past before you ordered it (7 minutes was the limit at the time).  Nowadays, they fix all the burgers in advance and keep them in steamers.  Bleck.  And they wonder why people complain?<P>But on a lighter note - I stopped at the McDonald's on I-95 just South of the Georgia/South Carolina Border (in Savannah) and got fan-damn-tastic service.  They were busy as hell, had a bus in the parking lot, and were fast, pleasant, efficient, and the food what hot, fresh and cooked right.  When I used to travel from NC to FL on a regular basis, Savannah GA was my half-way point, so I'd stop for a bite and gas.  I always got great service and good food there.  People complain about stuff when it's wrong, and rightly so.  I just wanted to add a testimonial about when it's done right. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||maryjane||09-17-2001||10:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stimpy:<BR><B>I can't remember the last time they got the order right for me.  I'm almost to the point of saying "Just give me $4 worth of food. It don't matter what I want, cuz I ain't gonna get it!"</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You must be on a diet of some sort. $4 won't buy much anymore||||reg||1
Z||000011||Fierowrecker||09-17-2001||10:40 PM||||I have given up on McD's and BK...<BR>Never get the order right, or if you order a shake, the shake machine is down...<BR>I go to Get 'em and go, fresh, flame broiled, and not nuked like the big guys...<BR>Plus it is Cheep! Not paying for a national name...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000012||fierohoho||09-18-2001||03:14 AM||||Like Joe Pesci's character said in "Lethal Weapon", "they f**k you at the drive through".<P>I always stay at the window no matter how busy they are until I have gone through the bag and checked my order.<P>If it's wrong I ask them to fix it, when they say pull over and we'll bring it out to you I say no I'll stay right here until it's right, I will refuse to move until they get it right.<P>Just realize, if you tick off someone making your food who makes minimum wage you may get a loogie burger. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pennockpic.gif"> ||||reg||1
