Z||000023||stimpy||09-19-2001||09:57 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B><BR>A bit off the path... <BR>Have you ever been to BK or McD's when the cash registers went down? <BR>It's truly sad watching them try to make change, without that little LED display to tell them how much.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Oh, I love it when, say your total comes to $5.63, you give the pimply faced dropout a $10 and after they enter the amount tendered on their register you say "Oh, I have 65¢."<BR>Talk about utter cofusion and abject horror. NOTE- Make sure you do this only when you have plenty of time to kill, as they will likely have to page a regional manager to tell them what to do. I've actually had these morons cancel out my order, then ask again what I wanted "So the drawer will come out balanced." (This was the Taco Bell's MANAGER who did that.) <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000024||frontal lobe||09-19-2001||08:12 PM||||They screw up, then they try to make it right by giving you free food NEXT time.  Well, that doesn't cut it.  Because now you are sitting at home without what you ordered and you want it NOW, not next time.  You went to "fast" food because you wanted it fast.  What are you going to do, get back in the car and drive back over?  That defeats the purpose of fast and convenient.||||reg||1
Z||000025||stsmithgt||09-19-2001||08:34 PM||||I thought onion rings were straight and taste like potatoe.?????  That's what I get most of the time too.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I'm too tired at the end of the day to climb out of my car more than once to go inside much less to remember to open the bag and inventory it. (there's only two items in the bag)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> ||||reg||1
