Z||000027||DJRice||09-19-2001||08:59 PM||||And what is the deal with numbering the combos if the cash register is not going to have a corresponding number on it as well?  I mean, I order a #3 supersized and the person has to turn around to look at the board to see that the #3 is the "Royale with Cheese."  If your going to put up a sign that says "#3 Combo: $3.49"  then the register should have a button that burger boy (or girl) can press that automatically prints "Royale with Cheese" on the screen.<P>Heres another one for you.  I went thru the drive thru at McDs one time and they got my order right....but on top of the order in the bag was <B><I>13</B></I> packages of Ketchup.  What in the burger flipping world is a person going to do with 13 ketchup packets in the car.  Thats like one pack of kecthup for every 2 fries or something.<P>I actually called back to the store after I got to where I was going to suggest to the manager that reducing the amount of ketchup that his people include in drive-thru orders might be a way to significantly increase profits...||||reg||1
